;; Wave evidence: v1.00.28 W8 — Final-claim cohort close and decision publication
;; Record-only companion to gsd-wave-reviews/v1.00.28-w8.rktd
;; and gsd-wave-validation/v1.00.28-w8.rktd.
(
(wave . "v1.00.28-w8")
(ticket . "#9633")
(implementation-sha . "faec39a2130806389b2a18ef0e754265215b3efc")
(delivery . "branch campaign/v1.00.28-w8 from fresh origin/main; squash-merge PR is owned by the coordinator; this trio is bound to the merge SHA at merge time")
(base . "origin/main 04637d835d33f887a29846a2f3c1855146151985; the branch carries W1-W7 campaign content already checkpointed on this branch's history")
(scope . "artifacts/ci-baseline/v1.00.28-final/{cohort.json,report.json,decision.md,SHA256SUMS} (new, checksummed), docs/reports/gsd-wave-{evidence,reviews,validation}/v1.00.28-w8.rktd (this trio); report.json is a byte-reproducible output of scripts/run-tests/cohort-report.rkt from cohort.json (--check), and the tooling plus its 132-case suite (74 cohort-report cases plus 58 companion regression cases) were delivered in the earlier checkpoints of this branch")
(what-was-done
 (mode . "final-claim per roadmap section 8 and Measurement Contract section 2: every roadmap row evaluated against its fixed threshold with coupled guards, one final verdict in the allowed vocabulary, no intermediate language, no target revision")
 (cohort . "the accumulation window closed with 8 of the expected 20 unique eligible PR head SHAs merged since C3; the shortfall is recorded explicitly (cohort-status \"open\", cohort-status-reason, expected-count 20, window-eligible-count 8, shortfall-count 12) instead of being papered over with unqualified or duplicate SHAs; every cohort SHA cell carries run IDs/URLs, timings, and lane outcome, and 4 lane-failed/cancelled SHAs are named mechanical exclusions (reason lane-run-failed, an allowed exclusion class) with run links, never silence")
 (report . "report.json is generated by scripts/run-tests/cohort-report.rkt from cohort.json and is byte-reproducible (--check regenerates and byte-compares: match); rows: class-a-fast-work-mass-delta -5.37 % (pass, its own measure class, never compared against Class B-D thresholds), fast-p50 282.5 s vs <= 115.0 s and fast-p95 294.95 s vs <= 135.0 s (target not achieved), pr-elapsed-p50 820.5 s vs <= 588.0 s and pr-elapsed-p95 850.3 s vs <= 735.0 s (target not achieved), security-runner-p50 709.0 s vs <= 240.0 s (target not achieved), workflows-runner-p50 715.5 s vs <= 220.0 s (target not achieved), prepared-env verified-restore 100 % (24/24 verified, >= 95 %, pass, 3 shards x 8 SHAs); coupled guards (inventory-accounted, reliability-non-regression, semantic-gate-equivalence, four-worker-isolation-proof, failure-truth) are present with references on every row that requires them, and reliability non-regression holds versus the recorded v1.00.27-c3 baseline (8 attempts, 0 failures, 0 cancellations, 0 reruns)")
 (decision . "decision.md states the cohort status, the accumulation window and shortfall, the 8-row verdict table, and ends in exactly one final verdict in the allowed vocabulary: PARTIAL WORKLOAD REDUCTION; FINAL TARGET NOT ACHIEVED; the Class A pass (work mass -5.37 %, a real but partial workload reduction on the W0 -> W7 census medians) plus the timing-target misses on an open, short cohort map to this verdict by the tooling's fail-safe mapping; every miss row names a next lever (fast-lane critical-path shrink, tail-shard rebalancing plus cache reuse, and re-run of the final cohort on 20 new PR head SHAs; a timing miss alone implies no queue rollback)")
 (honesty . "no SHA was requalified, duplicated, or dropped to improve numbers; thresholds 115/135/588/735/240/220/95 appear unchanged; failures and cancellations are ingested rows with run links; the four runtime counters remain 'unknown' with the W0 static wait-pattern proxy labeled as such, consistent with W7"))
(focused-results
 (cohort-check . "racket scripts/run-tests/cohort-report.rkt --check artifacts/ci-baseline/v1.00.28-final/report.json -> OK: report.json is byte-identical to the regeneration from cohort.json")
  (tests . "racket tests/test-ci-cohort-report.rkt -> green, exit 0, 132 cases across five groups (74 in the cohort-report group), including the fail-closed test-group, the Class A work-mass delta row, closed-cohort no-success strictness, and the --check positional-form regressions")
 (checksums . "sha256sum -c artifacts/ci-baseline/v1.00.28-final/SHA256SUMS -> cohort.json, report.json, decision.md OK")
 (decision-vocabulary . "grep -c of the three allowed verdict strings over decision.md yields exactly one verdict line, PARTIAL WORKLOAD REDUCTION; FINAL TARGET NOT ACHIEVED")
 (verify-lane . "the declared Verify command is coordinator-owned and runs at return; its components were exercised individually on this branch (cohort-report --check green, test-ci-cohort-report green, sha256sum -c OK, decision.md grep hit, branch campaign/v1.00.28-w8 != main)"))
(security-semantics . "untouched: no execute-* check, isolation root, worker-security contract, gate semantics, scheduler activation, or queue rollback decision was made; the wave publishes a measurement decision record only, and the scheduler default stays batch-ungrouped")
(result . "the final-claim decision record exists and is checksummed: 8-row verdict table with coupled guards, explicit 8-of-20 shortfall, one allowed-vocabulary final verdict (PARTIAL WORKLOAD REDUCTION; FINAL TARGET NOT ACHIEVED), report byte-reproducible from the cohort manifest, signed by an independent reviewer channel (APPROVE)"))
